  "conclusions": {
    "OQ-10_hourly_reach": "Ample. QQQ.O hourly serves 2026-06-01 onward (1152 bars). An expired weekly call (04-Sep) serves 2026-07-23 -> 2026-09-04 (256 bars), i.e. its whole listed life. A 10-week window is comfortably covered.",
    "OQ-11_bar_convention": "Bars are stamped at their START, in UTC, tz-naive. Proof: O_SEC_OFST=0 and C_SEC_OFST=3599 on essentially every bar; QQQ.O runs 08:00-23:00 UTC, which under start-stamping is exactly 04:00-20:00 ET, the US extended session; and the 19:00 UTC bar carries 55,942 trades against 3,966 in the 20:00 bar, which is the closing-hour surge. Therefore the 15:00-16:00 ET closing hour is the bar stamped 19:00 UTC WHILE EDT IS IN FORCE. Convert UTC -> America/New_York; never hardcode 19:00.",
    "OQ-12_strike_step": "$1.00 near the money, on both a live (18-Sep) and an expired (04-Sep) QQQ weekly: every integer strike 710..721 returns data; 712.50 and 717.50 return none.",
    "RIC_day_is_zero_padded": "The brief's rule 'DAY, not zero-padded (5, not 05)' is WRONG as LSEG resolves these today. All three of the brief's single-digit-day AAPL examples fail as written and succeed zero-padded. The repo's build_option_ric(), which uses {day:02d}, is correct.",
    "expired_suffix_is_not_immediate": "Two days after expiry the 11-Sep QQQ contracts still resolve ONLY under the LIVE form (no caret): QQQI112671500.U returns 24 bars, QQQI112671500.U^I26 returns nothing. The 04-Sep contracts (9 days out) resolve only under the caret form. A pull must try both forms and record which won.",
    "option_session_bars": "An option day has 8 hourly bars, 13:00..20:00 UTC. Under start-stamping that is 09:00-10:00 ET through 16:00-17:00 ET. The 20:00 UTC bar is AFTER the 16:00 ET equity close and carries real quotes, so 'the last bar of the session' is NOT the closing hour.",
    "live_capture_works": "A live, unexpired weekly (QQQI182671500.U) returns hourly BID/ASK history. Monday's entry can therefore be captured from the completed 19:00 UTC bar after the fact; it is not a real-time race.",
    "spot_context": "QQQ.O closed 714.88 on 2026-09-11; the window 2026-07-02..2026-09-11 has 50 sessions. 100 shares is about $71,500, so SD-3's round figure is $75,000."
  },
